# A driven app that dies of an error nobody caught must end, not hang: a driver has nothing else to
# tell it. `haxe tests/drive-crash-app/build.hxml` from the repo root; exits 0, printing `drive-crash-app: ok`.
# It starts this same program twice more as a child, each opening a window off every display (never
# activated) that throws from a haxe.Timer / from Host.StartTimer; each must exit non-zero within 10 s
# with the message on stderr. A child still alive after that is killed by its PID and the check fails.
-cp tests/drive-crash-app
-main Main
-lib haxeui-core
-lib haxeui-cs
-D haxeui_cs_drive
-D haxeui_cs_run
-debug
-cs tests/drive-crash-app/bin
-w -WAll
